# Release signing trust root for agent-sessions (#832).
#
# OpenSSH allowed_signers format, read verbatim by:
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=<this file> verify-tag <tag>
#
# ONE entry covers every FUTURE release — the property a per-release manifest
# structurally cannot provide, because a build can only ever carry entries for
# releases older than itself. This key outlives the releases it vouches for.
#
# Public key material only. Adding a line grants release authority; removing one
# revokes it for every build shipped afterwards. Custody, rotation and recovery:
# docs/release-signing.md (export-ignored — it names hosts and paths).
release@agent-sessions ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIOjW+gor5BTHMCjx6GWhCOJXdmR9Lei9elkzV7j++zbX agent-sessions release signing
